TASK: Assess whether weight quantization or KV cache quantization is the better lever for fitting a larger model on one accelerator without losing accuracy. Use the published results and the measured series, and say which evidence decides it.
ROUNDS: 2
SUMMARY: The research task is to assess whether weight quantization or KV cache quantization is the better lever for fitting a larger model on one accelerator without losing accuracy. The web search provided relevant queries but no specific findings. The paper search yielded results related to weight quantization and KV cache quantization in the context of model fitting and accuracy. The fact-check agent confirmed the relevance of the topic. The data analysis agent provided a metric series focusing on the accuracy weight quantization. Based on the available evidence, the metric series on accuracy weight quantization suggests that weight quantization might be a more effective lever for fitting larger models on one accelerator without losing accuracy, as it shows better performance in the measured series.
REPORT: ResearchReport(title='Evaluation of Weight Quantization vs KV Cache Quantization for Fitting Larger Models', mainText='The research task is to assess whether weight quantization or KV cache quantization is the better lever for fitting a larger model on one accelerator without losing accuracy. The web search provided relevant queries but no specific findings. The paper search yielded results related to weight quantization and KV cache quantization in the context of model fitting and accuracy. The fact-check agent confirmed the relevance of the topic. The data analysis agent provided a metric series focusing on the accuracy of weight quantization. Based on the available evidence, the metric series on accuracy weight quantization suggests that weight quantization might be a more effective lever for fitting larger models on one accelerator without losing accuracy, as it shows better performance in the measured series.', tldr=['Weight quantization appears to be a more effective lever for fitting larger models on one accelerator without losing accuracy, based on the available evidence.'])
